    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0164" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg144"/>

                <head>Mr. Dayton to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 535.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 9, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: As the most satisfactory mode of apprising
                    the foreign department here of your action in the case of Mr. Mansfield, our
                    consul at Tabasco, I read your despatch No. 618 to Mr. Drouyn de l’Huys. He
                    seemed much gratified with the kind and courteous manner in which you expressed
                    yourself in relation to his communication of the information he had received in
                    relation to the character and habits of our consul at that post.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WM. L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.,</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
